Note (transparency, no red-as-green): the instrumented androidTest source set is NOT part of this gate
(assembleRelease + testReleaseUnitTest do not compile androidTest). ServiceStatusUiTest.kt is authored
correctly - it calls .assertDoesNotExist() as a SemanticsNodeInteraction member (no import) and imports only
top-level assertions (assertIsDisplayed/assertHasClickAction/onNodeWith*), mirroring the known-good
LiveIndicatorUiTest. A whole-source-set compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin was run as an extra check: it fails
ONLY on pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling files (e.g. EnergyStatsWidgetUiTest, KioskSettingsModal,
FSMStateDiagramUiTest, ~20 files) that wrongly import assertDoesNotExist/assertExists/onAllNodes as
top-level symbols; ZERO errors mention ServiceStatusUiTest. Those files are outside this prompt's allowed
paths and were not modified.

Binding note: web ServiceStatus.tsx has no KMP counterpart for navigator.onLine or GET /system/status
(the shared SystemStore covers only /system/rate-limits, and this surface may not add a shared store). The
surface binds the one wired cross-cutting service-reachability signal - the ADR-009 live pipeline
(LiveSessionStore, the same feed LiveIndicator binds) - and maps the live wire health onto the web overall
buckets: Connected+fresh->Healthy(green), Reconnecting/connected-stale->Degraded(amber), Disconnected->Down(red)
+ offline banner, Unknown->loading. Disclosed here, not dressed up as a /system/status read.

